# Bootstrap + forms

## Styling

- Style UI with [Bootstrap 5.3](https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/) via `ui/src/styles.scss` (`form-control`, `form-select`, `form-label`, `btn`, grid, utilities).
- Use SCSS for component `styleUrl` / colocated styles. Override Bootstrap sparingly.
- Do not add Bootstrap’s JS bundle or invent a parallel design system when Bootstrap covers the need.

## Forms

- Existing screens use **Template-driven forms** (`FormsModule` / `[(ngModel)]`) — match that for auth and pick flows unless asked to migrate.
- Keep markup semantic: real `<label>` / accessible names.
- Mark required fields clearly; disable primary submit when required values are missing or the form is invalid.
- Do **not** introduce Signal Forms or Reactive Forms migrations unless the user explicitly asks.

## Example (template-driven)

```html
<label class="form-label" for="email">Email</label>
<input id="email" name="email" class="form-control" type="email" required [(ngModel)]="email" />
<button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" [disabled]="!email">Save</button>
```
